course: dictionary
lesson: 13326
title: Places in a castle
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some words name a place, and the words around them tell you what happens there. A guardroom is a room where soldiers or guards on duty stay, often near a gate. «The guards sat in the guardroom beside the castle gate.» The words guards, castle and gate are your clues: this is a room for guarding.
explain: The word has a second meaning, linked to prisons. «The thief was kept in the guardroom until the judge arrived.» Here the clue is thief. A guardroom can hold prisoners, but only for a short time, not for years.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The guards sat in the room beside the castle gate» still makes sense, so you are on the right track. If the sentence stops making sense, look for a different meaning.
fact: Guardroom is a noun: a guardroom, guardrooms.
fact: A guardroom is a room where soldiers or guards on duty stay, often near a gate.
fact: A guardroom can be in a castle or in a barracks, which is a building where soldiers live.
fact: «Guardroom» can also mean a room where prisoners are kept for a short time.
fact: In history lessons on castles, the guardroom is usually beside the gatehouse.
exercise: «The soldiers rested in the guardroom by the castle gate.» What is a guardroom? | *A room where soldiers on duty stay | A kind of small ship | A shop that sells maps | A tall tower on top of a hill
exercise: «The prisoner was kept in the guardroom for one night.» How long was the prisoner kept there? | Forever | *For a short time | For many years | Until the castle was built
exercise: «The guardroom was full of guards, watching the castle gate.» Which word is a clue that a guardroom is a room for guards? | castle | *guards | watching | gate
test: «The guardroom was full of soldiers who were on duty at the gate.» What does guardroom mean here? | A horse stable | A river crossing | A garden with flowers | *A room where soldiers on duty stay
test: «The prisoners were taken to the guardroom, then moved to a cell the next morning.» Why were they in the guardroom? | To paint the walls | *To be kept there for a short time | To be given a feast | To stay for ever
exam: In history lessons on castles, where is the guardroom usually found? | *Beside the gatehouse | In the top of the tallest tower | In the moat under the water | In the orchard
